      ],
      "course": "LK",
      "sourcePage": 40,
      "decision": "REVISE",
      "reason": "Current whole P requires own actual quantitative assay planning AND execution for methyl/ethylparaben, standards, matrix/selectivity and remeasurement. Correct fictional calibrations90c+20->24mg/L and75c+10 with factor18->36mg/L do not narrow that whole duty to a provided-data transfer. HE40 attaches quantitative determination to ascorbic acid; its separate paraben clause is usage of p-hydroxybenzoic acid esters. The historical P itself preserves that this is an authored analytical extension, not literal HE paraben closure. Do not require this whole as universal HE LK endpoint/target solely from that page; preserve actual ascorbic quantitative and paraben-use source duties and other jurisdictions/full authored P."
    }
